Revision history for AnyEvent::MCP

0.65  Fri 23 Oct 2026 22:41:32 CEST
	- fix mcp-webbrowser userscript title indicator duplicating prefixes on empty titles.
	- use built scripts in make test PATH, avoiding source shebangs and
	  accidentally installed helpers in rule management tests.
	- clarify browser execute code wrapper and reject function/symbol return
	  values instead of silently converting them to null.
        - fix many bugs in the testsuite.

0.62  Thu 22 Oct 2026 13:32:52 CEST
	- INCOMPATIBLE API CHANGE: mcp_getoptions now returns a hash reference instead of
          a key/value list.
	- Simple accepts server_name/server_version independently of the local
	  instance name, leaving server_info as an unmodified protocol override.
	- query multibroker children in parallel for tool and broker discovery,
	  preserving tool order and returning partial results after 15 seconds
	  instead of blocking on an unresponsive child.
	- accept a missing trailing slash on HTTP MCP endpoint URLs, working
	  around Claude's MCP connector wrongly dropping it from the configured URL,
          thus corrupting it.
	- allow omitted ports in reverse extension URLs, defaulting to port 80.
	- fix MCP client/server version fields serialized as JSON numbers in 0.61.

0.61  Thu 22 Oct 2026 08:57:42 CEST
	- resolve bind hostnames via AnyEvent::Socket instead of Socket::getaddrinfo.
	- honor user-selected file permissions and preserve them across replacements.
	- fix permission test fixture grants.
	- fix activity log timestamp formatting on older perl versions.
	- correct multibroker test tool count (including meta-instructions).
	- fix perl 5.12 syntax errors in mcp-fs and mcp-vim.

0.6  Wed 21 Oct 2026 20:43:20 CEST
	- 34k LOC of pure llm madness. but seems to work. yay.

0.0  Sat 03 Oct 2026 07:29:39 CEST
	- original version, an AnyEvent::HTTP clone.
